# Line endings: ONE place decides them, so the npm tarball is byte-reproducible.
#
# Why (measured, docs/release-playbook.md §7): this machine runs `core.autocrlf=true`, so the checkout
# wrote CRLF while the repository stores LF. `npm pack` reads the WORKING TREE, so 2.7.3 shipped at least
# one CRLF file in the tarball - content-equivalent, byte-different - and every diff review had to be read
# with `--ignore-cr-at-eol` (a single 1-line change in a 6000-line file looked like a 6000-line rewrite).
#
# Rule: text is LF everywhere (repo, checkout and tarball); binaries are never touched.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shipped text: stated explicitly as well, so a future `text=auto` misdetection cannot flip them.
*.js    text eol=lf
*.mjs   text eol=lf
*.cjs   text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.txt   text eol=lf
*.svg   text eol=lf
*.ps1   text eol=lf
*.tex   text eol=lf

# Binaries: never normalised, never diffed as text.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.zip   binary
*.gz    binary
*.7z    binary
*.exe   binary
*.dll   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
